# Renormalized Arithmetic Potential Theory of the Characteristic Circle

Umbrella for the theory of the renormalization data of the explicit formula: coupled counterterms
and the partner-rank law; the matched coupling of the archimedean place to the arithmetic point;
Gårding inequalities as finite-rank survivals;
covariance, the covariant counterterm `log N + O(1)` and the cost of the anomaly; the horizon
regulator, its polar divergence on uniform profiles, its unbounded rank on the torsion orbits, the
tensor law joining the two and its Hecke covariance without anomaly; the finite part `−2γ` on
uniform profiles and the tower forms on classes of any finite prime sieve, with one shared Euler
constant and a signed step-profile law; the actual matched finite-sieve operator, its complete
Blaschke basis, simple torsion-adjunction energies and compact shifted inverse; Ramanujan
quasimodes, uniform finite Ramanujan approximation at bounded defect, exact bounded spectral
counts, and simple eigenlines in the full integer prime spectrum;
the spectral ends of the atomic prime
form, the Liouville flip of the polar divergence and the matching law for sign gauges; the matched
stability law at atomic resolution; the laws in one statement.
See `RenormalizedArithmeticPotentialTheory/README.md`.
